    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/execute_requirement.py:215-220: `requirement_board.claim_started(...)` runs before `orchestrate_pre_authoring.status(...)`. The new spec requires the claim to follow durable initialisation, and the design says \"The beginning of `execute_requirement.advance`\". Neither requires or checks that state exists first.",
      "id": "advance-claims-without-durable-state",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "`advance` claims the card before checking that durable pre-authoring state exists. The delta ties the claim to a started Requirement (\"durably initialised\", \"every resume\"). A never-started Requirement passed to `advance` is projected to `In progress`, and `orchestrate_pre_authoring.status` then fails or reports not started. The card would then show occupied with no state behind it."
    }
